    "sampleProcessingProtocol": "Plant root material (200 mg) was ground in liquid nitrogen with 400 µl of extraction buffer (50 mM Tris-HCl, pH 8.0, 1 mM EDTA, 1 mM phenylmethylsulfonyl fluoride and 4 % [v/v] protease inhibitor cocktail [Roche]) using a pestle and mortar and centrifuged at 500 g for 10 min to obtain the supernatant.  Tag-switch method was performed in 1 mg of protein extract previously precipitated with TCA/acetone and resuspended in 200 µl of buffer containing 50 mM methylsulfonylbenzothiazole (MSBT) in 50 mM Tris-HCl (pH 8) amended with 2.5% SDS at 37°C for 60 min with agitation at 550 rpm. Unreacted MSBT was removed by acetone precipitation (1:5 v/v at -20 ºC overnight). After washing the pellet, the proteins were resuspended in 200 µl of buffer with 50 mM Tris-HCl (pH 8), 2.5% (w/v) SDS and 20 mM CN-biotin (Zhang et al., 2014) at 37°C for 4 h with agitation at 550 rpm. Proteins were then precipitated and pellets were washed with ice-cold acetone and resuspended in 50 mM Tris-HCl (pH 8). To purify the labeled proteins, the solution was incubated with 150 µl of magnetic streptavidin beads suspension (Sera-MagTM, Cytiva) for 1 h at room temperature in a tube rotator. The beads were intensively washed (five times) with Tris-HCl (pH 8), 600 mM NaCl, 1 mM EDTA and 0.5% Triton X-100 and the beads sedimented in a microfuge tube magnet. Bound proteins were eluted with 2% SDS, 30 mM biotin, 50 mM phosphate, 100 mM NaCl, 6 M urea, and 2 M thiourea solution for 15 min at room temperature, followed by 15 min at 96ºC as described (Aroca et al., 2017a). Magnetic beads were removed and the eluted proteins precipitated with TCA/acetone for mass spectrometry analysis.  The protein pellet was solubilized in the digestion buffer of 2% w/v sodium deoxycholate (SDC) in 100mM Tris-HCl pH 8.5 with 5mM tris(2-carboxyethyl)phosphine (TCEP) and 30mM 2-chloroacetamide (CAA). We added TCEP and CAA to be sure that any cysteine still free was anyway carbamidomethylated. Trypsin and Lys-C were added at ratios of 1:50 and 1:100 (w/w), respectively. Digestion was performed overnight at 37 °C overnight on ThermoMixer C (Eppendorf, Germany) with shaking at 1000 rpm. The SDC was removed via acid precipitation with trifluoroacetic acid (TFA). TFA was added till pH reached 2 and the peptides were desalted using an Oasis HLB plate, then dried and stored at −80 °C.",
